	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[The Badlands are a country of red rock, dry gullies and wind. South of {link:loch-modan}Loch Modan{/link} the mountains fall away into mesas and dust flats where little grows and less can drink. Crag coyotes run the plains, buzzards circle the canyons, and living stone walks where the earth itself has woken in anger. No kingdom holds this land. Yet it is crowded with claimants: dwarves of three banners, ogres, troggs, black dragons, a camp of goblins, a {link:gnomes}gnome{/link} with an experiment and an orcish fortress on the western cliffs. Most of them came for what lies beneath the northern hills. There the titans' vault of {link:uldaman}Uldaman{/link} has been opened, and everyone who has heard of it wants what it holds.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[The oldest thing in the Badlands is {link:uldaman}the vault of Uldaman{/link}, a work of the titans older than any dwarven hall. The {link:explorers-league}Explorers' League{/link} believes that its halls hold the answer to the question the dwarves most wish to answer: where their people came from. Around the vault, the League found stone urns and ruined terraces carved by hands that were not dwarven.

The later history of the land is a history of war. The {link:dark-iron-dwarves}Dark Iron Dwarves{/link} of {link:angor-fortress}Angor Fortress{/link} once held two lieutenants of {link:deathwing}Deathwing{/link} bound in the eastern ravine of {link:lethlor-ravine}Lethlor{/link}, and in the {link:second-war}Second War{/link} the {link:horde}Horde{/link} stood allied to the black dragon who was their master. No chronicle records how the land became so barren, or who first called it the Badlands.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "The Present Day",
			text = [=[Every faction in the Badlands is at war with at least two others. The Shadowforge clan of the {link:dark-iron-dwarves}Dark Irons{/link} holds {link:angor-fortress}Angor Fortress{/link} and digs into {link:uldaman}Uldaman{/link} in search of titan relics, and they answer to an envoy sent from the fires of {link:blackrock-mountain}Blackrock{/link} by {red:ragnaros}Ragnaros{/red} himself. They have already fallen on the League's dig, killed most of its workers and carried off its leader. The {link:troggs}troggs{/link} of the Stonevault clan have swarmed out of the vault and killed another League prospector in the south. The Dustbelcher ogres pick over the wreckage of the dwarven retreat. Black dragons nest in {link:lethlor-ravine}Lethlor Ravine{/link}, and the old seal that binds two of their kin is no longer thought safe.

The {link:horde}Horde{/link} holds {link:kargath}Kargath{/link} on the western cliffs. From there the Kargath Expeditionary Force wages a long war on the {link:blackrock-clan}Blackrock Clan{/link} and the Dark Irons across the mountain. The {link:alliance}Alliance{/link} has only a small camp of League survivors south of their lost dig, and they wait for help from {link:ironforge}Ironforge{/link}.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Inhabitants",
			text = [=[• {b}The {link:horde}Horde{/link} of {link:kargath}Kargath{/link}.{/b} {link:orcs}Orcs{/link}, trolls, {link:tauren}tauren{/link} and {link:forsaken}Forsaken{/link} who hold the western outpost and the road to {link:blackrock-mountain}Blackrock Mountain{/link}.
• {b}The {link:explorers-league}Explorers' League{/link}.{/b} A handful of dwarves who survived the fall of Hammertoe's dig.
• {b}The Shadowforge clan.{/b} Dark Iron dwarves of {link:angor-fortress}Angor Fortress{/link}, their golems and their fire-sworn envoy.
• {b}The Stonevault troggs.{/b} They hold the approaches to {link:uldaman}Uldaman{/link} and the southern dig sites.
• {b}The Dustbelcher ogres.{/b} They keep camps across the south and west, and they sell their clubs to anyone, then betray them.
• {b}The black dragonflight.{/b} Whelps and scorched guardians of the black dragons nest in {link:lethlor-ravine}Lethlor Ravine{/link}.
• {b}Wanderers and exiles.{/b} A goblin cook, a hunted smith, a gnomish mage and a madman who fled the {link:twilight-s-hammer}Twilight's Hammer{/link}.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "History",
			text = [=[• {b}The Makers.{/b} {link:uldaman}Uldaman{/link} was raised by the titans in an age before any mortal kingdom. What it was made to guard is still argued in the {link:hall-of-explorers}Hall of Explorers{/link}.
• {b}The Binding of the Drakes.{/b} The {link:dark-iron-dwarves}Dark Irons{/link} of {link:angor-fortress}Angor Fortress{/link} made a key they called the Sign of the Earth and used it to seal two of {link:deathwing}Deathwing{/link}'s lieutenants, the drakes {link:blacklash}Blacklash{/link} and {link:hematus}Hematus{/link}, beneath {link:lethlor-ravine}Lethlor Ravine{/link}. No chronicle records the year.
• {b}The Second War.{/b} The {link:horde}Horde{/link} fought beside Deathwing in the {link:second-war}Second War{/link}. {link:kargath}Kargath{/link}'s orcs now count that alliance as a stain on their honor.
• {b}The Digs.{/b} In recent years the League opened digs across the Badlands under Prospector Agmond and the explorer Hammertoe Grez. Both digs have now fallen.
• {b}The Present Day.{/b} The Shadowforge and the troggs dig in the vault. The League, the Horde and the {link:kirin-tor}Kirin Tor{/link} all send their agents to stop them, or to find what they seek first.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Lore of the Badlands",
			text = [=[• The survivors of Hammertoe's dig have learned that the desert plays tricks on the hungry, and that not everything glimpsed across the flats is really there.
• The League's smith swears that the hardest thing in the Badlands is not the {link:dark-iron-dwarves}Dark Irons{/link}. It is finding a meal.
• In the stomach of a great buzzard a hunter once found a pitted black box. Stamped on it were the words "Engine #19" and the name of the {link:ironforge}Ironforge{/link} Siege Brigade.
• The ogres of the Badlands wear so much scrap iron that the League's smith believes the old tales of siege engines in this land were true.
• A strange machine walks the southern Badlands, a thing of gears that answers to no one. It bears the title of a long-distance recovery unit, and no one knows what it was sent to recover.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Unrecorded",
			text = [=[No chronicle records how the Badlands became a desert, or the years in which {link:kargath}Kargath{/link} was raised and the {link:dark-iron-dwarves}Dark Irons{/link} built {link:angor-fortress}Angor Fortress{/link}.]=],
		},
	},
})

